    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d580">

                <pb facs="0507" n="495" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg495"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.3531/1585: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Tuck</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-09-12T16:00:00-03:00">September 12, 1940—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 4:12 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>405. Embassy’s telegram No. 402, September 12 [<hi rendition="#italic">11</hi>],
                    8 p.m. In a strictly confidential note dated September 12, the Minister for
                    Foreign Affairs<anchor n="39" xml:id="d580-f1"/> advises that the Argentine
                    Government is agreeable to having the proposed negotiations for a corn marketing
                    agreement initiated here immediately.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Tuck</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d580-f1" n="39" xml:id="d580-f1-content">
                <p>Julio A. Roca became Minister for Foreign Affairs on September 3, 1940.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
